#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""autofinish-run — a fresh, unattended `/finish` on one claude/* worktree, and how it ended.

    autofinish-run WORKTREE [--rule A|B|C|D|E|L|M] [--by sweep|override|typed|yolo|dnd|chain|ship] [--merge | --hold]
                   [--digest D] [--session ID] [--dry]
    autofinish-run notify [WORKTREE]      the run's own session: whom to message, and the text (below)

E1 of docs/autofinish-design-2026-10-02.md (D13): the runner. Whoever decides that a branch should
launch without the owner's wait — the sweep (rules A, B, D, E, L), `/autofinish` (C), a typed `/finish` handed
off cold (E7), the end of a `dispatch --yolo` or dnd build run (E12, `--by yolo|dnd`: the prompt becomes
`/finish <branch> --unattended --yolo|--dnd`) — calls this, and it returns at once.

The landing ladder (skipper-modes S3b; the owner, 2026-10-21: "dnd: I want to automerge as well"): before
the start, landing() reads the branch's mode from plan.json itself (bin/autofinish's landing_mode) and
decides whether this run may merge. `ask`: every launch but a person's stops at a ready PR. A mode
launch (`--by yolo|dnd`, or the sweep's rule M): `yolo` merges on any host bar the launcher's gates and
the repo's `autofinish_exclude` and `in_place`, `dnd` bar the held slice (bin/autofinish's held_slice:
money, a physical repo, a public publish, a deleted data file, `autofinish_exclude`), and a mode
lowered since holds — but a yolo launch with no mode at all in a `"merge": "auto"` repo, from a caller
without CLAUDE_UNATTENDED, keeps that standing yes (E12). A hold adds `--hold` to the prompt, denies
`bin/pr merge` to the run, writes `"hold": "<why>"` into the state, and a stop at step 11 is recorded
with gate `held` and the class (`stopped <branch> held held (<why>): …`), which helm's board cards.
`--by` itself grants nothing: the yes to merge is the mode, which only the owner raises
(helmlib.raise_refusal), so an unattended caller typing `--by yolo` gets what plan.json says. Defaults: --rule C, --by override (a person
calling it by hand is closest to `/autofinish`). --merge: the owner's `--merge` (/finish's: their explicit
yes to merge this branch's PR, given up front), carried into the run: the prompt becomes
`/finish <branch> --unattended --merge`, and on the build Mac step 11.4 then merges without asking. It
covers that one branch's PR only, and only a person gives it: `--by override` or `--by typed`; with
`--by sweep`, `chain` or `yolo` it is refused at once (exit 2) — the sweep and the chain have no
person's yes, and a yolo launch outside a `"merge": "auto"` repo stops at a held PR on purpose (E12).
So is any caller with CLAUDE_UNATTENDED set (exit 2): every dispatched run has it, and its allow rules
pass `bin/*` unseen, so a run the sweep started could otherwise launch another that merges. The label
is all that is checked otherwise, the caller's word that a person said yes. A chain relaunch of a
`--merge` run does not carry it, nor a sweep retry of one that died: either stops at the PR. --session: the caller's own session (E7's hook
passes the panel's), never a lock holder it is refused for. A skipper (SKIPPER_SCOPE set) is refused
--merge as an unattended run is: its yes is the keel's, carried as `--by ship`, never its own word.

A ship's launch (skipper-resilience S6; the yard component's "The merge default"): the yard's tick
(`wharf apply --once --all` on a scope's yard, bin/wharf's start_launch) launches a ship's `launch:
finish` block with `--merge --by ship --digest D` when the keel said merge, else `--hold`. `--by ship`
stands for a person's yes given at the keel — the owner's attended `wharf apply --yard`, whose blueprint
said `merge: yes` or nothing — so this re-reads it rather than trusting the label: D must be the pin
of exactly one un-ended ship on this Mac (plans/<id>/plan.json, helm's helmlib), its pinned copy
(plans/<id>/blueprint-<ship>.md, the committed text the yard read from origin) must be at D and not
say `merge: no`, the plan must record `laid_by.mode: attended` and no keel `merge: no`, and the
worktree must be in the pin's repo, on a block branch of that ship (a branch name alone repeats
across repos). `--by ship --hold` is the tick's launch where the keel said no: the same caller
refusal, no digest asked, nothing merged. The caller must be the tick, not a session: it
is refused under CLAUDE_UNATTENDED, SKIPPER_SCOPE, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, a DISPATCH_DEPTH past 0 or
a ship's own env (DISPATCH_SHIP, DISPATCH_PLAN: a block's command), exit 2 — launchd's tick has none
of them, and every dispatched run, skipper and block has one (the checkpoint hook denies a run that
strips CLAUDE_UNATTENDED). The mode still holds a ship launch in `ask`: `ship` is no person's label to
landing(). --hold: the caller holds the landing at a ready PR (the keel's no), whatever the mode —
the prompt gains `--hold` (finish_prompt), `bin/pr merge` stays denied, and the state's `hold` says
`the keel holds it (--hold)`; with --merge it is refused, the two ask opposite things. That hold is
sticky: any later launch of the worktree (a sweep retry of a run that died, a chain) keeps it, since
only the keel could lift it. A launch the ladder holds carries no `--merge` into its prompt.

A ship's lease (skipper-resilience S4): when DISPATCH_SHIP (or the older DISPATCH_PLAN) names a ship
that has one here (plans/<id>/skipper.json, helm's bin/leaselib.py), the caller's generation is
checked first — SKIPPER_GEN, else the lease's own session, else a plain shell — and any other is
refused, exit 4, with one event in the ship (none on --dry). No lease, no DISPATCH_SHIP, or helm not
installed: nothing is checked, as before.

Before the start, in this process, under `<git dir>/claude/autofinish.json.lock` (O_EXCL; one
older than START_LOCK_S is a start that died, taken over), so two callers never both pass the
refusals and both write:
  - no retry on the same tip: a worktree whose last run (its autofinish.json) was on this very
    commit is refused, whatever that run's outcome — a stop repeats itself on the same tip, and
    a run still going is not started twice. One exception: a run dispatch refused before any
    session existed (the run cap, its start lock: gate `refused`, `not-launched` before 2026-10-17 and
    read both ways) never ran, so it may start.
    `--by chain` (the chain manager's tick, orchestration B3) is judged by chain_refusal() instead:
    it relaunches only a tip whose last run stopped at `no-landing` with the network or sleep as the
    branch's last autofinished line (S4), at most CHAIN_RELAUNCHES times per tip (counted in
    `<git dir>/claude/autofinish-chain.json`), and a yolo launch it relaunches stays a yolo one;
  - the login (work-account E5, as `dispatch --account auto`; joined early on the owner's word,
    2026-10-08): `bin/account pick --repo <primary> --json` at start time, so a second login, first in
    the walk, takes the run unless the repo is on its deny list; the pick's CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR goes to
    the start (unset for the default dir, whose env must stay empty — bin/account's header), and
    `account` in the state and the log line names the row. Exit 3 from the pick (no row may run
    now) is a refusal with each row's reason; exit 4 (no registry) or an unreadable answer keeps
    the login this was started with, as before. A caller's CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR or
    CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is an explicit choice and is kept, no pick, unless that dir's row has
    a window locked or is parked (`limits --all --parked --json --cached`: parked, locked, or cooling
    down after an exhaustion):
    then the pick decides, and with no row to move to it refuses (2026-10-22). Kept:
    a panel session on the work login handing its /finish off cold, or a test (bin/autofinish's start_runner and dispatch --yolo's
    launch pass neither, so the sweep, the override and a yolo launch always pick). A pick past PICK_TIMEOUT (a probe hanging) falls back
    to `pick --cached`; --by typed picks `--cached` from the start (cold_prompt's 45 s, a hook's);
  - no lock taken from a session at work: owner.json naming a session that is not the caller,
    live in the registry (~/.claude/sessions, its pid alive) and not `idle` — busy, waiting on a
    dialog — is a refusal, whoever calls (review, 2026-10-05: a typed hand-off took one), unless
    the lock is marked `handover` (bin/pickup next; bin/wharf when it settles an Orca block, since
    2026-10-19: every session starts `sessionpipe wait` at SessionStart, so a finished builder
    reads `shell`, which counts as busy, and four launches were refused for it). A typed
    hand-off (--by typed) is refused, too, by any lock another session holds unexpired
    (checkpoint.py's held_by_other: seen under OWNER_TTL, not handed over): the owner typed /finish in
    one panel, and the branch is another's;
  - a session id is chosen, and `<git dir>/claude/autofinish.json` written with it (the contract
    the hooks read — `{"started", "session", "tip", "by", "rule", "window", "account", "ended",
    "outcome", "pr", "gate"}`, plus `"merge": true` for a `--merge` launch and `"hold": "<why>"` for a
    held one (S3b) — each key absent otherwise — and nothing else), then the worktree lock `owner.json` (hooks/common.py's
    write_owner) in that id's name: the session holds the lock from its first call (P8), and a
    panel session still open on the branch is refused its next write, with the reason.
    Should the detach fail after that, the lock is given back (the previous owner.json, or none)
    and the state ended `never-started` at gate `refused`, exit 1: nothing ran.
Then a detached child (a double fork and setsid: the caller's process group, a hook's or a
Bash call's, may be ended the moment the caller returns — dispatch's header, 2026-10-05):
  - the bundle — bin/pickup's context_bundle, the branch's prompts, its last asks and replies, its
    PR — at `<git dir>/claude/autofinish-bundle.md`: the conversation's record for /finish's
    learnings and open-items gates (design section 7). Written here, not before returning: it
    reads every transcript of the repo, seconds the caller should not wait;
  - `dispatch --start "/finish <branch> --unattended[ --yolo| --dnd][ --hold][ --merge]" <worktree> "finish · <topic>"`: Remote
    Control "finish · <topic> · laptop", a window tiled on Desktop 5 (bin/tiling), ended by dispatch-rc's watcher
    10 min after it goes idle — dispatch writes that `idle` into the run's record for every
    --start run, because this waiter blocks on the watcher and nobody picks a launch up again; a
    seeded branch run is kept the prompt cache's hour instead (2026-10-06), and is ended before
    this start (`dispatch-rc end-warm`; a busy one stops it — D2 of
    docs/dispatch-warm-hour-2026-10-08.md); opus (dispatch's default — no model flag here: a model is
    chosen in bin/gate or a script bin/test_gate.sh names); `--permission-mode auto` with dispatch's allowlist
    plus what /finish runs (Agent, EnterWorktree, git, the contract's `check:` as written on the
    primary's main, the modules' bin/* and libexec/* in the regatta main checkout, carried.py), and dispatch's denied list minus
    `git push` and bin/pr's launch verbs: checkpoint.py and the repo's pre-push judge those by
    ref. No `--background`: dispatch's default holds — background tasks off
    (CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_BACKGROUND_TASKS=1), so a Bash call past BASH_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS (30 min)
    is killed, not backgrounded; /finish starts its check as `nohup bin/check … &` inside one call and polls
    its summary (skills/finish step 1; bin/check reads main's check line when CLAUDE_UNATTENDED is set). Every CLAUDE* variable is stripped first but the two that name the account
    (lessons/claude-code.md: a child of a session saves no transcript) — dispatch's screen
    runner strips them too, its headless fallback does not;
  - it waits for dispatch to return, which is the watcher's end.
After the end, in `finally`, whatever happened before:
  - the lock is released if it still names this session, and a `finishing` marker removed (R29:
    a `-p` exit once left owner.json naming a dead session; the watcher frees it too, this does
    not rely on that). A waiter ended while its session still runs ends that session first:
    a lock and a marker freed under a live /finish would let the checkpoint hook commit into its
    rewrite;
  - the outcome, read from the transcript's last reply, never from a return code (`launched` was
    `landed` before rename S4; every reader takes both, common.LAUNCHED_OUTCOMES):
      launched       a DONE closing line (common.ending), `Shipped:` or a `rollback:` line, and no
                     ⚠ anywhere → pr N from `merged #N`, the PR link, the Shipped line, or GitHub
      stopped        any ⚠ line, whatever else the reply says (a stop may well name `merged #57`
                     or a rollback: review, 2026-10-05); gate `G<n>` from the first ⚠ line
                     (`⚠ step 4 — …`, as the skill's --unattended paragraph asks), else from its
                     words, else `stop`; no ⚠ and no launch: `nothing-to-land` or `no-landing`
                     (an ending /finish never writes, R16)
      never-started  no reply in the transcript: gate `never-started` and the screen's last lines
                     (the watcher's hardcopy), or `refused` when dispatch refused to start;
  - autofinish.json updated (`ended`, `outcome`, `pr`, `gate`); a stop posted as one comment on the
    branch's PR through hooks/common.py's api; a line in `<common git dir>/claude/autofinished`
    (`launched <branch> #N` — no number when none was read —, `stopped <branch> <gate> <line>` or
    `never-started <branch> <line>`: the shapes bin/autofinish's header gives, design section 7);
    and one line in ~/Library/Logs/claude-weekly/autofinish-<date>.log,
    `<iso> run <repo> <branch> <outcome> …`.

A runner that dies — the Mac lost power, the process was killed — never reaches that `finally`
(2026-10-06: two rule-D runs, a laptop at 1 %). bin/autofinish's sweep asks `dead()` about every
worktree whose state says started with no outcome, and `bury()` writes what the `finally` would
have, as outcome `died` (docs/autofinish-died-2026-10-07.md):
  - dead: the waiter itself is gone (its pid and start time in autofinish-waiter.json — while it
    runs, nothing else is asked: a Mac asleep before dispatch wrote its record is not a death);
    then neither its claude (the pid with its recorded start time: a reused pid is not it) nor
    dispatch's watcher runs, and dispatch wrote no end; or dispatch ended it PRE_START_S ago and
    no outcome followed (the waiter died); or no dispatch record PRE_START_S after the start.
    A run dispatch ended is recorded with the outcome its transcript gives (record(), as the
    waiter would have) — a launch or a stop is not a death;
  - autofinish.json ended `died` (gate null), the lock released and a `finishing` marker removed
    when the lock still names the dead session (or none does), one comment on the PR, a line
    `<iso> died <branch> <tip7> <dispatch log's last line>` in `autofinished` and
    `<iso> run <repo> <branch> died session=… tip=… rule=… by=… account=… — <that line>` in the day's log.
    The override marker stays: the branch is judged again, and a rule-C branch needs it for that.
  A died run's tip is no "same tip" refusal here: bin/autofinish retries it once (its header).

The sessions it works on are told (the owner, 2026-10-18: "message every open/active session it works
on … and provide details of the session that's running it"). At the start, before the lock changes
hands, the live sessions open on the worktree — bin/autofinish's sessions_on(): the lock's holder,
the last prompter, any whose cwd is inside it; a typed hand-off's caller left out, it handed the
branch over — go into `<git dir>/claude/autofinish-notify.json` ({"session", "targets", "ts",
"told"}). A write that fails is said and skipped, never a failed start. SendMessage is a model tool
and no CLI verb sends one (2.1.302), so the run's own session sends them, as its first act under
`/finish --unattended` (skills/finish), each send judged by the classifier — no allow rule:

    autofinish-run notify [WORKTREE]

prints, per target still live, `SendMessage to <name>` (with its cwd where another live session
shares the name) and the text: the branch is taken, and the run's session id, how ListAgents lists
it (every run is named `run-finish`, so by its cwd too), its Remote Control name as dispatch
recorded it, account, rule, start, tip, record and log. A target with no inbox, or gone since, is
named and skipped: checkpoint.py's once-notice at its next prompt carries the run's session,
account and rule. So does a send across logins that SendMessage refuses — unproven either way
(docs/session-asks-2026-10-09.md, B0c), which is why the day's log line says `asked=`, not sent.
Only the run's own session gets the lines (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID; unset is refused), only while
the run is under way, and once (`told`). Exit 0, also with nothing to send.

The run's own output (dispatch's log and this child's) goes to
~/Library/Logs/claude-weekly/<date>-dispatch-finish-<topic>.log. --dry prints what would be
written and run — the state, the lock, the bundle's head, and dispatch's own dry run, claude's
whole command line included — and writes nothing.

Exit: 0 started (or --dry), 1 the detach failed (nothing ran, the lock given back), 2 usage or not
a claude/* worktree, 3 refused (same tip, a run going, another start under way, a lock in use, no
account may run it now), 4 the ship's lease refuses the caller's generation (DISPATCH_SHIP; S4).
Tests (bin/test_autofinish_run.sh) replace dispatch's commands with DISPATCH_CLAUDE, _SCREEN and the
rest; AUTOFINISH_DISPATCH replaces dispatch itself, AUTOFINISH_ACCOUNT bin/account (dispatch's
DISPATCH_ACCOUNT; the tests mostly run the real one on a fixture registry), AUTOFINISH_API_STUB names a Python file whose
`api()` stands in for common.api. Python 3.9, stdlib only.
"""
import argparse
import contextlib
import datetime
import glob
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import io
import json
import os
import pathlib
import re
import shlex
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import traceback
import urllib.parse
import uuid

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(HERE), "lib"))
import core_path  # noqa: E402 — the regatta core (C2); none: one line, exit 2
core_path.require()
import common  # noqa: E402

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
LOGS = os.path.join(HOME, "Library", "Logs", "claude-weekly")
RUNS = os.path.join(LOGS, "run-seed-runs")  # dispatch's record of each run
DISPATCH = os.environ.get("AUTOFINISH_DISPATCH") or os.path.join(HERE, "dispatch")
# account is lighthouse's (G12): without it, no pick — the run keeps the login it was started with.
ACCOUNT = os.environ.get("AUTOFINISH_ACCOUNT") or (str(common.tool("account") or "") or None)
STATE, BUNDLE, RECORD = common.AUTOFINISH_RUN, "autofinish-bundle.md", common.AUTOFINISHED
START_LOCK = STATE + ".lock"
WAITER = "autofinish-waiter.json"   # {"pid", "start"}: the detached waiter, for dead()
NOTIFY = "autofinish-notify.json"   # {"session", "targets", "ts"}: who `notify` tells (the header)
KEYS = ("started", "session", "tip", "by", "rule", "window", "account", "ended", "outcome", "pr", "gate")
OPTIONAL_KEYS = ("merge", "hold", "keel_hold", "eff_mode")   # written only when set: a launch without --merge or a hold keeps the file it always had
# eff_mode: the mode landing() judged a mode launch by — the branch's, or `yolo` for E12's standing yes
# (no mode, a "merge": "auto" repo, a person's caller) — which bin/pr's re-check reads where the branch
# has no mode now, never a bare `by: yolo` (follow-ups item 4)
LAND_BY = ("yolo", "dnd")   # the mode launches (skipper-modes S3b): `--by` names the mode, plan.json decides
PERSON_BY = ("override", "typed")   # a person's own launch: mode ask does not hold it (landing())
MERGE_BY = PERSON_BY + ("ship",)   # whose yes --merge may carry: a person's, or the keel's for a ship (the header)
SHIP_HOLD = "the keel holds it (--hold)"   # the state's `hold` for a --hold launch (S6)
REFUSED = common.REFUSED   # the gate of a start dispatch refused before any session; was "not-launched"
REFUSED_GATES = common.REFUSED_GATES   # read both forever: old run records and dated logs keep the old word
DIED = "died"
DIED_WHY = "the runner died before an outcome: the Mac lost power or the process was killed; nothing merged"
PRE_START_S = 600   # a state this young with no run record yet: its child may still be writing the bundle
START_LOCK_S = 130   # the refusals and the writes take a second, the pick at most PICK_TIMEOUT + 5 s (a caller
                     # with its own dir first `which`, 10 s, and its row, 5 s, both cached), ending a warm
                     # run up to 90 s (start(), capped): 125 s at worst; an older lock's holder died
PICK_TIMEOUT = 15    # a probe takes ~4 s, and the sweep's fresh pick seconds before left the cache warm; a
                     # hang falls back to --cached. bin/autofinish's start_runner waits 120 s for all of
                     # this; cold_prompt's typed hand-off 45 s (it picks --cached, ends a warm run in 30 s)
COMMENT_CAP = 3000   # characters of the ⚠ block in the PR comment
# The account variables stay (bin/account); DISPATCH_* (or, from before the rename, RUN_SEED_*) of a calling run would make this one part of
# its chain (DEPTH, BRIEF) or delete its launchd job (LABEL) — dispatch's own list, plus the chain's.
KEEP_CLAUDE = ("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR", "CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN")
DROP_DISPATCH = tuple(p + v for p in ("DISPATCH_", "RUN_SEED_") for v in ("LABEL", "LOG", "YEAR", "DEPTH", "BRIEF"))
NAME_RE = re.compile(r"^claude/(?:[a-z0-9-]+/)?\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}-(?P<topic>.+)$")  # pickup's NAME_RE
# --by chain (the chain manager's tick, orchestration B3): which stops it may relaunch, and how often.
# The patterns are bin/stalls.py's NET_RE and LOGIN_RE, character for character (test_helm.sh compares
# them): the tick judges S4 with one copy and this file lifts its refusal with the other.
S4_RE = re.compile(r"^(?:API Error\b|Your computer went to sleep|.{0,60}\bECONNREFUSED\b)")
LOGIN_RE = re.compile(r"Not logged in|/login\b|OAuth token|authentication_error", re.I)
CHAIN = "autofinish-chain.json"   # {"tip", "sessions"}: the chain relaunches on that tip (chain_refusal)
CHAIN_RELAUNCHES = 2                 # D4 = C (the owner, 2026-10-14): two retries per step, a launch's tip included
ROLLBACK_RE = re.compile(r"^.*\brollback:\s.*$", re.M)
MERGED_RE = re.compile(r"\bmerged #(\d+)")
PULL_RE = re.compile(r"/pull/(\d+)\b")
HASH_RE = re.compile(r"#(\d+)\b")
STEP_RE = re.compile(r"\bstep (\d+)", re.I)
# a ⚠ line that names no step: the gate by its words, first match wins (the skill's steps → design's G-numbers)
GATE_WORDS = (("open item", "G4"), ("owns the checkout", "G0"), ("lock", "G0"),
              ("another session", "G10"), ("review", "G1r"), ("deploy", "G1"), ("live", "G1"),
              ("check", "G1"), ("github", "G5"), ("merge", "G11"), ("push", "G11"), ("rebase", "G11"))

if os.environ.get("AUTOFINISH_API_STUB"):  # the tests' GitHub: find_pr and the comment go through it
    _spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("api_stub", os.environ["AUTOFINISH_API_STUB"])
    _stub = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)
    _spec.loader.exec_module(_stub)
    common.api = _stub.api


def load_bin(name):
    """A script in bin/ as a module (no .py, sometimes a dash: no plain import)."""
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(name.replace("-", "_"), os.path.join(HERE, name))
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader))
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def now_iso():
    return datetime.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat(timespec="seconds")


def git(where, *args):
    r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", where, *args], capture_output=True, text=True)
    return r.stdout.strip() if r.returncode == 0 else ""


class Tree:
    """The worktree, read from git — never from the caller's cwd."""

    def __init__(self, path):
        self.path = git(path, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel")
        self.gitdir = git(path, "rev-parse", "--absolute-git-dir")
        common_dir = git(path, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir")
        self.common = common_dir
        self.primary = os.path.dirname(common_dir) if common_dir.endswith("/.git") else ""
        self.branch = git(path, "symbolic-ref", "--quiet", "--short", "HEAD")
        self.tip = git(path, "rev-parse", "HEAD")
        m = NAME_RE.match(self.branch)
        self.topic = m.group("topic") if m else self.branch.rsplit("/", 1)[-1]
        self.repo = os.path.basename(self.primary)
        self.state_dir = os.path.join(self.gitdir, "claude")
        self.window = "finish · %s" % self.topic   # dispatch adds " · <machine>" for Remote Control
        # fixed at the start: a run that crosses midnight keeps one file
        self.runlog = os.path.join(LOGS, "%s-dispatch-finish-%s.log" % (datetime.date.today().isoformat(), self.topic))

    def problem(self):
        if not self.path or not self.gitdir:
            return "not a git worktree"
        if not self.branch.startswith("claude/"):
            return "on %s, not a claude/* branch" % (self.branch or "a detached HEAD")
        if not self.primary or os.path.realpath(self.path) == os.path.realpath(self.primary):
            return "the primary checkout: a runner works in the branch's own worktree"
        return None


def read_state(t):
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(t.state_dir, STATE)) as f:
            st = json.load(f)
        return st if isinstance(st, dict) else None
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def contract(st):
    """The keys autofinish.json carries: KEYS always, OPTIONAL_KEYS only when set."""
    return dict({k: st.get(k) for k in KEYS}, **{k: st[k] for k in OPTIONAL_KEYS if st.get(k)})


def write_state(t, st):
    """The contract's keys, in its order, nothing else; through a rename, so a hook never reads half."""
    os.makedirs(t.state_dir, exist_ok=True)
    path = os.path.join(t.state_dir, STATE)
    tmp = "%s.%d" % (path, os.getpid())
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump(contract(st), f, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)
        f.write("\n")
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def log(line):
    """One line in the day's autofinish log — the dry run's file and shape."""
    os.makedirs(LOGS, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(LOGS, "autofinish-%s.log" % datetime.date.today().isoformat()), "a") as f:
        f.write(line.rstrip("\n") + "\n")


def run_record(sid):
    """(path, state) of dispatch's record of the run with this session id, or (None, None)."""
    for path in glob.glob(os.path.join(RUNS, "*.%s.json" % sid[:8])):
        try:
            with open(path) as f:
                st = json.load(f)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        if st.get("session") == sid:
            return path, st
    return None, None


def run_live(sid):
    """True while dispatch's run of this session is not over: its claude or its watcher still
    running and no end written (dispatch-rc's unfinished())."""
    path, _ = run_record(sid)
    if not path:
        return False
    rc = load_bin("dispatch-rc")
    st = rc.load(path)
    if st.get("ended"):
        return False
    return rc.same(st) or (isinstance(st.get("watcher"), int) and not rc.watcher_gone(st))


def last_stop(t):
    """The detail of this branch's last line in `autofinished` when that line is a stop, else None."""
    entries = [e for e in common.autofinished(t.common) if e["branch"] == t.branch]
    return entries[-1]["detail"] if entries and entries[-1]["outcome"] == "stopped" else None


def chain_runs(t):
    """The sessions `--by chain` started on this worktree's tip, from CHAIN (any other tip's are void)."""
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(t.state_dir, CHAIN)) as f:
            d = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return []
    return list(d.get("sessions") or []) if isinstance(d, dict) and d.get("tip") == t.tip else []


def chain_spent(t, prev):
    """The chain relaunches spent on this tip: CHAIN's sessions less the one dispatch refused before any
    session existed (refused) — that start is always the `prev` of the next one, so start()
    drops it from CHAIN then, and a refused start is never counted once a later one runs."""
    return [s for s in chain_runs(t) if not (prev and s == prev.get("session") and prev.get("gate") in REFUSED_GATES)]


def chain_refusal(t, prev):
    """Why the chain manager's tick may not relaunch this tip, or None (orchestration B3, chain-manager
    E3, D4 = C). The one refusal it lifts — no retry on the same tip — only for the one cause it is
    for: the last run on this very tip stopped at `no-landing` and the branch's last autofinished
    line says the network or sleep stopped it (S4_RE, anchored at the stop text's start, as
    bin/stalls.py's NET_RE: a WAITING line that quotes an API error is not one — R4). At most
    CHAIN_RELAUNCHES of them per tip; a chain start dispatch refused before any session (refused)
    leaves the stop in place and is not counted against the tip."""
    if not prev or prev.get("tip") != t.tip:
        return ("a chain relaunch is for a launch stopped on this tip, and its last run was on %s"
                % (str((prev or {}).get("tip") or "none")[:7]))
    if not prev.get("ended"):
        return "a run on this tip started %s (session %s) has not ended" % (
            prev.get("started"), str(prev.get("session"))[:8])
    started = chain_spent(t, prev)
    if not (prev.get("outcome") == "stopped" and prev.get("gate") == "no-landing") and prev.get("gate") not in REFUSED_GATES:
        return "its run on this tip ended %s at %s, not stopped by the network — no chain relaunch" % (
            prev.get("outcome"), prev.get("gate") or "no gate")
    gate, _, text = (last_stop(t) or "").partition(" ")
    if gate != "no-landing" or not S4_RE.match(text) or LOGIN_RE.search(text):
        return "the branch's last autofinished line is no network or sleep stop — no chain relaunch"
    if len(started) >= CHAIN_RELAUNCHES:
        return "%d chain relaunches on this tip already (%s) — raised, not retried" % (
            len(started), ", ".join(s[:8] for s in started))
    return None


def refusal(t, prev, by=None):
    """Why no run starts now, or None."""
    if by == "chain":
        return chain_refusal(t, prev)
    if not prev:
        return None
    if prev.get("tip") == t.tip and prev.get("gate") not in REFUSED_GATES and prev.get("outcome") != DIED:
        if not prev.get("ended"):
            return "a run on this tip started %s (session %s) has not ended" % (
                prev.get("started"), str(prev.get("session"))[:8])
        return ("its run on this tip (%s) ended %s, %s%s — no retry on the same tip" % (
            t.tip[:7], prev.get("ended"), prev.get("outcome"),
            " at %s" % prev["gate"] if prev.get("gate") else ""))
    if not prev.get("ended") and prev.get("session"):
        if run_live(prev["session"]):
            return "a run is going on this worktree (session %s, tip %s)" % (
                prev["session"][:8], str(prev.get("tip"))[:7])
        try:
            started = datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(prev.get("started") or "").timestamp()
        except ValueError:
            started = 0
        if not run_record(prev["session"])[0] and time.time() - started < PRE_START_S:
            return "a run was started %s and has not reached dispatch yet" % prev.get("started")
    return None


def same_session(a, b):
    """A full id and its first 8 (a trailer's) are the same session."""
    a, b = str(a or ""), str(b or "")
    return bool(a and b) and (a == b or (min(len(a), len(b)) >= 8 and (a.startswith(b) or b.startswith(a))))


def open_sessions(t, caller=None, typed=False):
    """The live sessions open on this worktree now (bin/autofinish's sessions_on, by the lock's
    holder, the last prompter and cwd): the ones `notify` tells. Read before the lock changes hands."""
    af = load_bin("autofinish")
    state = pathlib.Path(t.state_dir)
    ids = {s for s in ((common.read_owner(state) or {}).get("session"), af.queue_session(state)) if s}
    return sorted({e["sessionId"] for e in af.sessions_on(pathlib.Path(t.path), ids)
                   if not (typed and same_session(e["sessionId"], caller))})


def write_targets(t, sid, targets, told=None):
    path = os.path.join(t.state_dir, NOTIFY)
    tmp = "%s.%d" % (path, os.getpid())
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump({"session": sid, "targets": targets, "ts": now_iso(), "told": told}, f, indent=1)
        f.write("\n")
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def notify_text(t, st, me):
    """The message: what happened to the branch, then the run — enough to find, watch or reach it.
    Every name is read back, never built: the Remote Control name from dispatch's record (it spells
    the host as the config keys do), the run's name from the registry — which is `run-finish` for every
    run (dispatch's -n), so the session id and the worktree go with it."""
    rc = (run_record(st["session"])[1] or {}).get("rc_name") or common.autofinish_window(st, t.branch)
    name = (me or {}).get("name")
    reach = ("ListAgents lists it as %s, cwd %s" % (name, t.path)) if name else "ListAgents lists it by its cwd, %s" % t.path
    return ("autofinish picked up this session's branch %s: a fresh unattended /finish is launching it now. "
            "The run: session %s (%s), window and Remote Control \"%s\", account %s, rule %s (by %s), "
            "started %s on tip %s. It holds this worktree's lock, so writes here are refused until it ends; "
            "its outcome shows here at the next prompt and on the PR. Record %s; log %s. "
            "To stop it, type in its window or Remote Control session (/autofinish off stops only the next start). "
            "No reply needed."
            % (t.branch, st["session"], reach, rc, st.get("account") or "unchanged", st.get("rule"), st.get("by"),
               common.iso_clock(st.get("started")), (st.get("tip") or "")[:7], os.path.join(t.state_dir, STATE),
               runlog_of(t, st)))


def notify(argv):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="autofinish-run notify")
    ap.add_argument("worktree", nargs="?", default=".")
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)
    t = Tree(os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(args.worktree)))
    if t.problem():
        print("autofinish-run notify: %s: %s" % (args.worktree, t.problem()), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    st = read_state(t) or {}
    me = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID")
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(t.state_dir, NOTIFY)) as f:
            n = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        n = {}
    if not st.get("session") or st.get("ended"):
        print("nothing to send: no autofinish run is under way on %s" % t.branch)
        return 0
    if not same_session(me, st["session"]):
        # closed when unknown: anyone else sending these would speak as the run
        print("nothing to send: the run on %s is session %s, not this one (%s)"
              % (t.branch, st["session"][:8], me[:8] if me else "no CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID"))
        return 0
    if n.get("session") != st["session"] or not n.get("targets"):
        print("nothing to send: no other session was open on %s when the run started" % t.branch)
        return 0
    if n.get("told"):
        print("nothing to send: the lines were printed at %s already" % common.iso_clock(n["told"]))
        return 0
    live = {e["sessionId"]: e for e in load_bin("autofinish").live_sessions()}
    text = notify_text(t, st, live.get(st["session"]))
    asked, skipped = [], []
    for sid in n["targets"]:
        e = live.get(sid)
        if not e:
            skipped.append("%s — ended since the start" % sid[:8])
            continue
        name = e.get("name") or sid
        if not e.get("messagingSocketPath"):
            skipped.append("%s — binds no inbox; checkpoint's notice tells it at its next prompt" % name)
            continue
        # ListAgents: a bare name is the address unless two rows share it (asklib's same_named, K2)
        twins = [x for x in live.values() if e.get("name") and x.get("name") == e["name"] and x["sessionId"] != sid]
        print("SendMessage to %s" % name + ("  — %d other live session(s) share the name: send to the ListAgents "
                                            "row whose cwd is %s, with its [ref]" % (len(twins), e.get("cwd"))
                                            if twins else ""))
        asked.append(sid[:8])
    if asked:
        print("with this text, word for word:\n\n%s\n" % text)
    for s in skipped:
        print("skip %s" % s)
    try:
        write_targets(t, n["session"], n["targets"], told=now_iso())
    except OSError:
        pass
    # asked=, not sent=: the model makes the sends, and one across logins may be refused (unproven, B0c)
    log("%s run %s %s notify session=%s asked=%s%s" % (now_iso(), t.repo, t.branch, st["session"][:8],
                                                       ",".join(asked) or "-", " skipped=%d" % len(skipped) if skipped else ""))
    return 0


def lock_refusal(t, caller, typed):
    """Why the worktree's lock is not this run's to take, or None. The registry is bin/autofinish's
    reader (its pid and procStart test), so both judge a live session alike."""
    lock = common.read_owner(t.state_dir)
    holder = (lock or {}).get("session")
    if not holder or same_session(holder, caller):
        return None
    live = next((e for e in load_bin("autofinish").live_sessions() if same_session(e["sessionId"], holder)), None)
    # handed over (`pickup next`, or wharf once the yard settled the block): free while the holder
    # is idle or `shell` — a finished builder still runs the Session-tab waiter, so it reads `shell`.
    # Busy, it may still be in its last turn (worker-done, then the Stop checkpoint): refused (review, 2026-10-19)
    if lock.get("handover") and (not live or live.get("status") in ("idle", "shell")):
        return None
    if live and live.get("status") != "idle":
        return "the worktree's lock is held by session %s, live and %s" % (holder[:8], live.get("status") or "with no status")
    if typed and not lock.get("handover") and time.time() - (lock.get("seen") or 0) < common.OWNER_TTL:
        return ("the worktree's lock is held by session %s (seen %d min ago), not the one that typed /finish"
                % (holder[:8], (time.time() - (lock.get("seen") or 0)) // 60))
    return None


def take_start_lock(t):
    """The path of `autofinish.json.lock`, now ours, or None while another start holds it."""
    os.makedirs(t.state_dir, exist_ok=True)
    path = os.path.join(t.state_dir, START_LOCK)
    for _ in range(2):
        try:
            fd = os.open(path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o644)
        except FileExistsError:
            try:
                if time.time() - os.path.getmtime(path) < START_LOCK_S:
                    return None
                os.remove(path)
            except OSError:
                pass  # gone meanwhile: the next try takes it
            continue
        os.write(fd, str(os.getpid()).encode())
        os.close(fd)
        return path
    return None


def give_back(t, sid, before, st):
    """The detach failed after the lock and the state were written: the lock as it was (or none),
    and the state ended never-started at `refused` — nothing ran, so the tip may start again."""
    path = os.path.join(t.state_dir, common.OWNER_FILE)
    if (common.read_owner(t.state_dir) or {}).get("session") == sid:
        if before is None:
            try:
                os.remove(path)
            except OSError:
                pass
        else:
            tmp = "%s.%d" % (path, os.getpid())
            with open(tmp, "w") as f:
                f.write(before)
            os.replace(tmp, path)
    st.update(ended=now_iso(), outcome="never-started", gate=REFUSED)
    write_state(t, st)


class NoAccount(Exception):
    """No row of the registry may run this now; args[0] is each row's reason."""


def account_pick(t, cached=False):
    """(label, dir, why) of the login the session runs on (header, the login). dir: the
    CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR to start with, "" for the default login (unset), None to leave the env as
    it is. Raises NoAccount on the pick's exit 3."""
    if os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN"):
        # the token outranks any dir (bin/account's header): `account which` reads only the dir
        return "oauth-token", None, "the caller's CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, kept"
    cfg = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR")
    if not ACCOUNT and not cfg:
        return None, None, "no account tool (lighthouse not installed) — the login this run was started with"
    cooling = False
    if cfg:
        try:
            if not ACCOUNT:
                raise OSError("no account tool")
            r = subprocess.run([ACCOUNT, "which"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
            label = r.stdout.strip() if r.returncode == 0 else ""
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
            label = ""
        # ~/.claude set explicitly is the default login, which runs logged out unless unset
        # (bin/account's header) — bin/autofinish passes it for a pick of the default row
        default = os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser(cfg)) == os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser("~/.claude"))
        cooling = cooling_down(cfg)
        if cooling:
            label = cooling
        else:
            # no spaces: the run lines are key=value, split on whitespace
            return re.sub(r"\s+", "_", label or cfg), "" if default else None, "the caller's CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, kept"
    cmd = [ACCOUNT, "pick", "--repo", t.primary, "--json"]
    try:
        r = common.run_group(cmd + (["--cached"] if cached else []), PICK_TIMEOUT)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        try:  # a probe that hangs: the cached readings decide, as a dry run's do
            r = common.run_group(cmd + ["--cached"], 5)
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
            return None, None, "account pick failed (%s) — the login this run was started with" % type(e).__name__
    except OSError as e:
        return None, None, "account pick failed (%s) — the login this run was started with" % e
    try:
        d = json.loads(r.stdout)
    except ValueError:
        d = None
    if r.returncode == 4:
        return None, None, "no account registry here — the login this run was started with"
    if r.returncode == 3 and isinstance(d, dict):
        raise NoAccount("; ".join("%s: %s" % (l, w) for l, w in d.get("skipped") or []))
    if r.returncode or not isinstance(d, dict) or not d.get("account"):
        return None, None, "account pick failed (%s) — the login this run was started with" % (
            (r.stdout or r.stderr).strip()[:120] or "exit %d" % r.returncode)
    why = d.get("reason") or ""
    if cfg and cooling:
        why = "the caller's %s is cooling down, so picked: %s" % (label, why)
    return d["account"], (d.get("env") or {}).get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR", ""), why


def cooling_down(cfg):
    """The label of the row whose home is CFG when it is parked or a window of it is locked, else None. A caller's
    login is an explicit choice over the soft ceilings, never over a lock: a panel session left on
    a cooling login handed every landing it launched to that login (yard-s2, 2026-10-22, the work login
    held till 11:00). The row is read by its home, not from pick's `skipped`: pick stops at the
    first eligible row and never judges the rest, and `which` names no default row (the review)."""
    if not ACCOUNT:
        return None
    try:
        r = common.run_group([ACCOUNT, "limits", "--all", "--parked", "--json", "--cached"], 5)
        rows = json.loads(r.stdout)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired, ValueError):
        return None
    home = os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser(cfg))
    for a in rows if isinstance(rows, list) else []:
        if not isinstance(a, dict) or not a.get("home") or os.path.realpath(a["home"]) != home:
            continue
        lim = a.get("limits") if isinstance(a.get("limits"), dict) else {}
        if a.get("enabled") is False or lim.get("locked") or str(a.get("why") or "").startswith("cooling down"):
            return re.sub(r"\s+", "_", str(a.get("label") or cfg))
    return None


def use_account(cfg):
    """The pick's dir into this process's env, so the start and the transcript's reader follow it."""
    if cfg is None:
        return
    if cfg:
        os.environ["CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR"] = cfg
    else:
        os.environ.pop("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR", None)


def finish_prompt(branch, by=None, merge=False, hold=None):
    """The prompt the run starts with (the header's)."""
    return "/finish %s --unattended" % branch + (" --%s" % by if by in LAND_BY else "") + (" --hold" if hold else "") \
        + (" --merge" if merge else "")


def _lander():
    """bin/autofinish as a module: landing_mode and held_slice, the ladder's one copy (S3b). None when
    it will not load (its wharf peer missing exits at import): the caller then holds."""
    try:
        return importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("autofinish_lander", os.path.join(HERE, "autofinish")).load_module()
    except BaseException:  # noqa: B036 — SystemExit included: a missing peer is a hold, never a crash
        return None


def main_of(t):
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(t.primary, ".claude", "workflow.json")) as f:
            return json.load(f).get("main") or "main"
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        return "main"


def landing(t, by, rule):
    """(hold, mode, eff) for this launch — the landing ladder (skipper-modes S3b), read here from plan.json
    (bin/autofinish's landing_mode), never from the caller: `--by` is a label any caller may type, and
    every dispatched run's allow rules pass bin/* unseen (AGENTS.md's unattended-caller trap). `hold` is
    why the run stops at a ready PR, or None when it may merge:
      - mode `ask`: every launch holds but a person's (`override` or `typed`, no CLAUDE_UNATTENDED);
      - a mode launch (`--by yolo|dnd`, or rule M): held_slice under the mode now — `yolo` merges bar the
        launcher's own gates and the repo's `autofinish_exclude`/`in_place`, `dnd` bar the held slice, any
        other mode holds (a taken answer never lands there, yolo-veto D1) — except that a yolo launch
        with no mode at all (a run from before the mode) in a `"merge": "auto"` repo keeps its standing
        yes (E12), and only from a caller without CLAUDE_UNATTENDED: a lowered mode is a mode, and a run
        typing `--by yolo` is no person (landing review 3, 4c);
      - a ship launch (`--by ship`, the keel's yes): held_slice as a mode launch, under `yolo` when the
        ship has no landing mode — the yes was given to a blueprint before any diff, so the launcher's
        gates and the repo's `autofinish_exclude`/`in_place` still hold it (S6's finish review);
      - anything else: None, today's rules (a plain /finish --unattended, step 11.4 by host).
    `eff` is the mode a mode or ship launch was judged by (None for any other), for autofinish.json's
    `eff_mode`: bin/pr judges the launch again by it where the branch has no mode by then."""
    af = _lander()
    if af is None:
        return ("the lander's judge did not load (bin/autofinish)"
                if by in LAND_BY or rule == "M" or by == "ship" else None), None, None
    mode = af.landing_mode(t.branch, t.primary or None)[0]  # with the repo, as the sweep's verdict reads it
    # `ship` is the keel's yes to merge, not a person at the keyboard: mode ask holds it too
    person = by in PERSON_BY and not os.environ.get("CLAUDE_UNATTENDED")
    if mode == "ask" and not person:
        return "mode ask — nothing lands by itself", mode, None
    if by not in LAND_BY and rule != "M" and by != "ship":
        return None, mode, None
    if by == "ship":
        eff = mode if mode in af.LAND_MODES else "yolo"
    else:
        eff = mode if mode in af.LAND_MODES else ("yolo" if by == "yolo" and mode is None and merge_auto(t)
                                                  and not os.environ.get("CLAUDE_UNATTENDED") else mode)
    try:
        return af.held_slice(t.primary, t.path, main_of(t), eff), mode, eff
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — what it cannot read is a hold
        return "the held slice could not be read (%s)" % type(e).__name__, mode, eff


# the module tools /finish names ("Where the tools are"), each with the verb where only one is meant
FINISH_TOOLS = ("wharf-runs/bin/pickup", "wharf-runs/bin/check", "wharf-runs/bin/autofinish-run",
                "wharf-runs/bin/rc-hosts", "keel/bin/keel", "keel/bin/paste-paths", "keel/bin/owed",
                "atlas/bin/knowledge-commit", "wharf/libexec/pr", "wharf/bin/review-gate",
                "wharf/hooks/carried.py", "regatta/bin/regatta which", "helloworld/bin/helloworld check")


def regatta_main():
    """The regatta main checkout this core belongs to (never a worktree, which /finish removes), as
    an absolute path, or None (a plugin install: no checkout)."""
    root = common.regatta_root()
    if not root:
        return None
    gd = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(root), "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir"],
                        capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()
    top = os.path.dirname(gd) if gd.endswith("/.git") else str(root)
    # the root as the caller spells it when it is the main checkout: git resolves links (/var is
    # /private/var on macOS), and a rule must read as the session types the path
    return os.path.abspath(str(root)) if os.path.realpath(top) == os.path.realpath(str(root)) else top


def start_cmd(t, sid, dry=False, by=None, merge=False, hold=None):
    """dispatch --start, with E1's lists. The FINISH_TOOLS rules are the modules' in
    the regatta main checkout (/finish runs its tools there since B14b, 2026-10-23, which deleted the
    overlay's shims; B14a's D1-A), in the two spellings a session types them in: under `~/` and the
    absolute path. The deny list wins over them: a held launch keeps `pr merge` denied. No regatta
    checkout (a plugin install): no such rule, and the classifier judges those calls like any other."""
    # No allow rule for the contract's check command: since D1-A (2026-10-13) a branch may launch
    # an AGENTS.md change unwatched, and an allow rule approves before the classifier looks, so
    # the check line would become pre-approved code (code review, 2026-10-13). The classifier
    # judges the check like any command; a slower run, never a wrong one.
    # No allow rule for SendMessage either (`notify`, the header): a bare one would let text in the
    # bundle steer any live session unseen; the classifier judges each send (review, 2026-10-18)
    allow = ["Agent", "EnterWorktree", "Bash(git:*)"]
    top = regatta_main()
    roots = []
    if top:
        rel = os.path.relpath(top, HOME)
        roots = (["~/" + rel] if not rel.startswith("..") else []) + [top]
    for root in roots:
        # one rule per tool the finish skill names, never modules/*/bin/* wholesale: that pre-approved
        # every module tool, live-state writers (clock, knowledge-home, scope-pass) and the core's
        # `regatta pr merge` among them, which no deny pattern matched (the B14b landing review)
        for tool in FINISH_TOOLS:
            allow += ["Bash(%s/modules/%s*)" % (root, tool), "Bash(python3 %s/modules/%s*)" % (root, tool)]
    prompt = finish_prompt(t.branch, by, merge, hold)
    cmd = [DISPATCH, "--start", prompt, t.path, t.window,
           "--session-id", sid]   # opus: dispatch's default (header)
    for a in allow:
        cmd += ["--allow", a]
    lift = ["Bash(git push:*)", "Bash(*bin/pr ready*)", "Bash(*bin/pr merge*)",
            "Bash(*libexec/pr ready*)", "Bash(*libexec/pr merge*)",
            "Bash(*regatta pr ready*)", "Bash(*regatta pr merge*)"]
    if hold:
        # a held launch (landing(): mode ask, the dnd slice, a mode lowered since, E12's yolo outside a
        # `"merge": "auto"` repo) stops at a ready PR. The skill says so; this makes it so — prose alone
        # did not hold once (bin/dispatch, idea-redaction, 2026-10-04)
        lift.remove("Bash(*bin/pr merge*)")
        lift.remove("Bash(*libexec/pr merge*)")
        lift.remove("Bash(*regatta pr merge*)")
    for d in lift:
        cmd += ["--undeny", d]
    return cmd + (["--dry-run"] if dry else [])


def merge_auto(t):
    """The repo's standing yes: `"merge": "auto"` in .claude/workflow.json on origin/<main> (main's
    name read from the primary's copy), as /finish step 11.4 reads it. Unreadable: no."""
    try:
        cfg = json.loads(git(t.path, "show", "origin/%s:.claude/workflow.json" % main_of(t)) or "{}")
    except ValueError:
        return False
    return isinstance(cfg, dict) and cfg.get("merge") == "auto"


def start_env(t):
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items()
           if not (k.startswith("CLAUDE") and k not in KEEP_CLAUDE) and k not in DROP_DISPATCH}
    env["DISPATCH_LOG"] = t.runlog
    return env


def bundle_text(t):
    """pickup's context bundle for the branch, as `pickup open --here` prints it."""
    try:
        from pathlib import Path
        pk = load_bin("pickup")
        root = pk.repo_root(Path(t.path))
        data = pk.collect(root, fetch=False)
        b = pk.resolve(t.branch, data["branches"])
        s = b["sessions"][0] if b["sessions"] else None
        buf = io.StringIO()
        with contextlib.redirect_stdout(buf):
            pk.context_bundle(b, data, s)
        return buf.getvalue()
    except Exception as e:  # pickup's Stop included: the run goes on from git alone
        return ("(no bundle: pickup could not read %s — %s: %s. The branch's commits carry its "
                "prompts: git log --reverse --format='%%h %%s%%n%%b' main..HEAD)\n" % (t.branch, type(e).__name__, e))


def write_bundle(t, st):
    path = os.path.join(t.state_dir, BUNDLE)
    with open(path, "w") as f:
        f.write("# The conversation's record for /finish %s --unattended\n\n" % t.branch)
        f.write("Written %s by bin/autofinish-run for session %s, tip %s — read it as the old "
                "session's record (design section 7): its prompts, its last asks and replies.\n\n"
                % (now_iso(), st["session"], t.tip[:7]))
        f.write(bundle_text(t))
    return path


# ---- after the end -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def transcript(sid):
    dirs = {os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR") or os.path.join(HOME, ".claude"), os.path.join(HOME, ".claude")}
    for d in dirs:
        hits = glob.glob(os.path.join(d, "projects", "*", sid + ".jsonl"))
        if hits:
            return hits[0]
    return None


def last_reply(sid):
    """The session's last assistant text (a subagent's sidechain is not the session's), or None."""
    text = None
    try:
        with open(transcript(sid), errors="replace") as f:
            for line in f:
                if '"assistant"' not in line:
                    continue
                try:
                    rec = json.loads(line)
                except ValueError:
                    continue
                if rec.get("type") != "assistant" or rec.get("isSidechain"):
                    continue
                content = (rec.get("message") or {}).get("content")
                if isinstance(content, list):
                    said = "\n".join(c.get("text", "") for c in content
                                     if isinstance(c, dict) and c.get("type") == "text").strip()
                    text = said or text
    except (OSError, TypeError):
        return None
    return text


def tail_lines(path, offset=0, n=8):
    try:
        with open(path, errors="replace") as f:
            f.seek(offset)
            lines = [l.rstrip() for l in f if l.strip().strip("\0")]
    except (OSError, TypeError):
        return []
    return lines[-n:]


def gate_of(warn):
    m = STEP_RE.search(warn)
    if m:
        return "G%s" % m.group(1)
    low = warn.lower()
    return next((g for w, g in GATE_WORDS if w in low), "stop")


def read_outcome(t, sid, log_from):
    """(outcome, pr, gate, lines): lines is what the log, the record and a comment quote."""
    path, rec = run_record(sid)
    if not path:
        return "never-started", None, REFUSED, tail_lines(t.runlog, log_from) or ["(dispatch wrote nothing)"]
    text = last_reply(sid)
    if not text:
        shown = tail_lines(path + ".screen.txt", 0, 15)   # dispatch-rc's hardcopy of a never-busy screen
        return "never-started", None, "never-started", shown or tail_lines(t.runlog, log_from) or [
            "(no reply, no screen: %s)" % rec.get("end_reason", "?")]
    lines = [l.strip() for l in text.splitlines() if l.strip()]
    # a ⚠ anywhere is a stop, read before any launch marker: a stop report may well name another
    # PR's merge or quote a rollback line (review, 2026-10-05: `merged #57` read as launched)
    warn = next((i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if "⚠" in l), None)
    if warn is not None:
        block = [l for l in lines[warn:] if not common.closing_kind(l)]
        return "stopped", None, gate_of(lines[warn]), block
    rollback = ROLLBACK_RE.search(text)
    if common.ending(text)[0] == "done" and (rollback or "Shipped:" in text):
        m = MERGED_RE.search(text) or PULL_RE.search(text) or HASH_RE.search(
            next((l for l in lines if "Shipped:" in l), "")) or HASH_RE.search(text)
        pr = int(m.group(1)) if m else merged_pr(t)
        return "launched", pr, None, [rollback.group(0).strip()] if rollback else lines[-1:]
    # the gate tokens are persisted, so they keep their word; /finish's text says either (rename S4)
    gate = "nothing-to-land" if ("Nothing to land" in text or "Nothing to launch" in text) else "no-landing"
    return "stopped", None, gate, lines[-1:]


def slug(t):
    """owner/name of origin as configured (not `get-url`, which expands insteadOf)."""
    return common.repo_slug(git(t.primary, "config", "--get", "remote.origin.url"))


def merged_pr(t):
    """The launched PR's number when the reply names none: the newest merged PR of this head."""
    s = slug(t)
    if not s:
        return None
    st, prs = common.api("GET", "/repos/%s/pulls?state=closed&per_page=5&head=%s:%s"
                         % (s, s.split("/")[0], urllib.parse.quote(t.branch, safe="")))
    hit = next((p for p in prs or [] if isinstance(p, dict) and p.get("merged_at")), None) if st == 200 else None
    return hit.get("number") if hit else None


def comment(t, st, outcome, gate, lines):
    """The stop, on the branch's PR. Returns (pr number or None, what happened)."""
    s = slug(t)
    if not s:
        return None, "no comment: origin is not on GitHub"
    pr = common.find_pr(s, t.branch)
    if not pr:
        return None, "no comment: no open pull request for %s" % t.branch
    what = {"never-started": "never started", DIED: "runner died"}.get(outcome) or "stopped at %s" % gate
    head = ("**autofinish %s** — `%s`, session `%s`, tip `%s`, rule %s, started by %s at %s."
            % (what, finish_prompt(t.branch, st.get("by"), st.get("merge"), st.get("hold")), st["session"], str(st.get("tip") or t.tip)[:7], st.get("rule"), st.get("by"),
               st.get("started")))
    quoted = "\n".join(lines)
    if len(quoted) > COMMENT_CAP:
        quoted = quoted[:COMMENT_CAP - 1] + "…"
    if outcome == DIED:  # its words first, then dispatch's log as it was left
        body = head + "\n\n" + DIED_WHY + ".\n\n" + ("```\n%s\n```" % quoted) + (
            "\n\nThe sweep may judge this branch once more — not once this PR is out of `WIP:`, nor "
            "a branch the runner had already curated locally; a second death on this tip waits for a prompt. "
            "The transcript, if any, is session `%s` on %s." % (st["session"], common.host_name()))
    else:
        body = head + "\n\n" + ("```\n%s\n```" % quoted if outcome == "never-started" else quoted) + (
            "\n\nNothing retries on this tip. A new commit can be started again; the transcript is "
            "session `%s` on %s." % (st["session"], common.host_name()))
    code, _ = common.api("POST", "/repos/%s/issues/%d/comments" % (s, pr["number"]), {"body": body})
    return pr["number"], ("commented on #%d" % pr["number"] if code == 201
                          else "comment on #%d refused (HTTP %s)" % (pr["number"], code or "none"))


def release(t, sid):
    """The lock if it is still this session's, and a `finishing` marker. Returns what was done."""
    done = []
    lock = common.read_owner(t.state_dir)
    if lock and lock.get("session") == sid:
        try:
            os.remove(os.path.join(t.state_dir, common.OWNER_FILE))
            done.append("lock released")
        except OSError as e:
            done.append("lock NOT released: %s" % e)
    marker = os.path.join(t.state_dir, "finishing")
    if os.path.exists(marker):
        try:
            os.remove(marker)
            done.append("finishing marker removed")
        except OSError as e:
            done.append("finishing marker NOT removed: %s" % e)
    return done


def end_live_run(sid):
    """A run still going when its waiter is ended (SIGTERM, a crash here): ended the way
    `dispatch --end` ends one, so nothing frees its lock under it. True when it was live."""
    path, _ = run_record(sid)
    if not path:
        return False
    rc = load_bin("dispatch-rc")
    st = rc.load(path)
    if st.get("ended") or not rc.same(st):
        return False
    reason = "ended with its autofinish waiter"
    cur = rc.load(path)
    cur["ending"] = reason
    rc.save(path, cur)
    if rc.end_session(st):
        rc.finish(path, rc.load(path), reason)
    return True


def wait_for_end(t, st, cmd):
    """The detached child: bundle, start, wait; then, whatever happened, the lock and the record."""
    def term(signum, _frame):
        raise SystemExit(128 + signum)
    signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, term)
    signal.signal(signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIG_IGN)   # a closing terminal is not an end
    sid, rc, why = st["session"], None, None
    try:  # its pid for dead(); autofinish.json's keys are the hooks' contract, so a file of its own
        rc_mod = load_bin("dispatch-rc")
        with open(os.path.join(t.state_dir, WAITER), "w") as f:
            json.dump({"session": sid, "pid": os.getpid(), "start": rc_mod.proc_start(os.getpid())}, f)
    except Exception:
        traceback.print_exc()
    try:
        log_from = os.path.getsize(t.runlog)
    except OSError:
        log_from = 0
    p = None
    try:
        print("%s autofinish-run: bundle %s" % (now_iso(), write_bundle(t, st)), flush=True)
        p = subprocess.Popen(cmd, env=start_env(t))
        rc = p.wait()
    except BaseException as e:  # SystemExit from SIGTERM included: the finally below is the point
        signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIG_IGN)   # a second TERM must not cut the cleanup short
        why = "the waiter ended: " + ("signal %s" % e.code if isinstance(e, SystemExit) else type(e).__name__)
        if not isinstance(e, SystemExit):
            traceback.print_exc()
        # dispatch gets a TERM it can clean up after (its start lock, its plist), not subprocess.call's KILL
        if p and p.poll() is None:
            p.terminate()
            try:
                p.wait(timeout=30)
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                p.kill()
    finally:
        signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIG_IGN)
        notes = []
        try:
            if why and end_live_run(sid):
                notes.append("its live session ended")
        except Exception:
            traceback.print_exc()
        notes += release(t, sid)
        try:
            record(t, st, log_from, rc, why, notes)
        except Exception:
            traceback.print_exc()
            # still an end in the state: an `ended: null` would read as a run going on forever
            try:
                if not (read_state(t) or {}).get("ended"):
                    st.update(ended=now_iso(), outcome="stopped", gate="error")
                    write_state(t, st)
            except Exception:
                traceback.print_exc()
            log("%s run %s %s error session=%s — %s" % (now_iso(), t.repo, t.branch, sid[:8],
                                                         "the outcome could not be recorded; " + "; ".join(notes)))


def record(t, st, log_from, rc, why, notes):
    sid = st["session"]
    outcome, pr, gate, lines = read_outcome(t, sid, log_from)
    if why and outcome not in common.LAUNCHED_OUTCOMES:
        lines = [why] + lines
    if st.get("hold") and outcome == "stopped" and gate == "G11":
        # the held landing (S3b): the gate says so, and the line names the class whatever the model
        # wrote, so the board's held card (helm_render) reads it from `autofinished`, not from prose
        gate, lines = "held", ["held (%s): %s" % (st["hold"], lines[0] if lines else "a ready PR waits for the owner's tap")] + lines[1:]
    said = ""
    if outcome not in common.LAUNCHED_OUTCOMES and gate not in REFUSED_GATES:
        pr, said = comment(t, st, outcome, gate, lines)
    st.update(ended=now_iso(), outcome=outcome, pr=pr, gate=gate)
    write_state(t, st)
    # /autofinish's marker has done its job once a run ended: left behind, a `now` marker would
    # have the Stop hook judge the branch again at every later turn's end (E3's note)
    if gate not in REFUSED_GATES:
        try:
            os.unlink(os.path.join(t.state_dir, common.AUTOFINISH_OVERRIDE))
        except OSError:
            pass
    first = lines[0] if lines else ""
    # `<iso> <outcome> <branch> <detail>`: the shape hooks/common.py's autofinished() parses, and
    # its phrase reads an empty launched detail as `#?` — never a `#None`
    if outcome in common.LAUNCHED_OUTCOMES:
        detail = "%s %s%s" % (outcome, t.branch, " #%s" % pr if pr else "")
    elif outcome == "never-started":
        detail = "never-started %s %s" % (t.branch, first)
    else:
        detail = "stopped %s %s %s" % (t.branch, gate, first)
    line = st["ended"] + " " + detail.rstrip()
    if gate not in REFUSED_GATES:   # nothing ran: no record for the session start to report
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(t.common, "claude"), exist_ok=True)
        with open(os.path.join(t.common, "claude", RECORD), "a") as f:
            f.write(line + "\n")
    extra = [x for x in (said, "dispatch exit %s" % rc if rc not in (0, None) else "") + tuple(notes) if x]
    log(common.RUN_END % (
        st["ended"], t.repo, t.branch, outcome, " gate=%s" % gate if gate else "",
        " pr=#%s" % pr if pr else "", sid[:8], t.tip[:7], st.get("rule"), st.get("by"), st.get("account") or "-",
        first[:300], "; " + "; ".join(extra) if extra else ""))


def runlog_of(t, st):
    """The dispatch log a run wrote to: named for the day it started (Tree's is today's)."""
    day = str(st.get("started") or "")[:10] or datetime.date.today().isoformat()
    return os.path.join(LOGS, "%s-dispatch-finish-%s.log" % (day, t.topic))


def waiter_alive(state_dir, sid):
    """True while the run's waiter (autofinish-waiter.json, same session) still runs."""
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(state_dir, WAITER)) as f:
            w = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return False
    if not isinstance(w, dict) or w.get("session") != sid or not isinstance(w.get("pid"), int):
        return False
    return load_bin("dispatch-rc").running(w["pid"], w.get("start"))


def dead(t, st, now=None, state_dir=None):
    """Why this worktree's run died without an outcome, or None: no run, an ended one, or one that
    may still live. Never a guess on the dying side — a waiter still running, a watcher not yet
    recorded, or a dispatch end its waiter is still recording, is no death."""
    if not st or st.get("ended") or not st.get("session") or not st.get("started"):
        return None
    if state_dir and waiter_alive(state_dir, st["session"]):
        return None
    now = time.time() if now is None else now
    try:
        started = datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(st["started"]).timestamp()
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        started = 0
    path, _ = run_record(st["session"])
    if not path:
        if now - started < PRE_START_S:
            return None
        return "no dispatch record %d min after its start" % ((now - started) // 60)
    rc = load_bin("dispatch-rc")
    try:
        rec = rc.load(path)
        age = now - os.path.getmtime(path)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    if rec.get("ended"):
        ended = rec["ended"] if isinstance(rec["ended"], (int, float)) else now - age
        if now - ended < PRE_START_S:
            return None
        return "dispatch ended the run %d min ago (%s) and no outcome was recorded" % (
            (now - ended) // 60, rec.get("end_reason") or "no reason")
    if rc.same(rec):
        return None
    w = rec.get("watcher")
    if isinstance(w, int):
        if not rc.watcher_gone(rec):
            return None
    elif age < PRE_START_S:
        return None   # no watcher recorded yet: dispatch may still be starting it
    return "claude (pid %s) and its watcher (pid %s) are gone, and dispatch wrote no end" % (
        rec.get("pid"), w if isinstance(w, int) else "never recorded")


def bury(t, why):
    """Record the dead run as the waiter's `finally` would have: the state, the lock, the PR, the
    record and the log. Under the start lock, the state read again: None when another start or
    an end got there first, else the log line written."""
    held = take_start_lock(t)
    if not held:
        return None
    try:
        st = read_state(t)
        if not st or st.get("ended"):
            return None
        sid = st["session"]
        holder = (common.read_owner(t.state_dir) or {}).get("session")
        notes = release(t, sid) if not holder or holder == sid else [
            "the lock is session %s's now: left as it is" % str(holder)[:8]]
        _, rec = run_record(sid)
        if rec and rec.get("ended"):  # the session ended, only its waiter died: its reply is the outcome
            record(t, st, 0, None, None, notes + ["recorded after its waiter died (%s)" % why])
            return "%s run %s %s recorded after its waiter died — %s" % (now_iso(), t.repo, t.branch, why)
        last = tail_lines(runlog_of(t, st), 0, 1)
        lines = last or ["(its dispatch log %s is empty or gone)" % runlog_of(t, st)]
        pr, said = None, ""
        try:
            pr, said = comment(t, st, DIED, None, lines + ["(%s)" % why])
        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — GitHub down is no reason to leave the run undead
            said = "no comment: %s" % type(e).__name__
        st.update(ended=now_iso(), outcome=DIED, pr=pr, gate=None)   # ended after the comment: the
        write_state(t, st)                                           # retry's GitHub quiet starts here
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(t.common, "claude"), exist_ok=True)
        with open(os.path.join(t.common, "claude", RECORD), "a") as f:
            f.write("%s died %s %s %s\n" % (st["ended"], t.branch, str(st.get("tip"))[:7], lines[0]))
        extra = [x for x in [said, why] + notes if x]
        line = "%s run %s %s died session=%s tip=%s rule=%s by=%s account=%s — %s; %s" % (
            st["ended"], t.repo, t.branch, sid[:8], str(st.get("tip"))[:7], st.get("rule"), st.get("by"),
            st.get("account") or "-", lines[0][:300], "; ".join(extra))
        log(line)
        return line
    finally:
        try:
            os.remove(held)
        except OSError:
            pass


def detach(fn, out_path):
    """fn() in a grandchild in its own session, its output appended to out_path; returns at once.
    Raises when no grandchild was made: the fork failed, or the child could not setsid or fork."""
    sys.stdout.flush()
    sys.stderr.flush()
    pid = os.fork()
    if pid:
        _, status = os.waitpid(pid, 0)
        if not os.WIFEXITED(status) or os.WEXITSTATUS(status):
            raise OSError("the detaching child ended with status %d" % status)
        return
    try:
        os.setsid()
        if os.fork():
            os._exit(0)
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)
        fd = os.open(out_path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_APPEND, 0o644)
        null = os.open(os.devnull, os.O_RDONLY)
        os.dup2(null, 0)
        os.dup2(fd, 1)
        os.dup2(fd, 2)
        fn()
        code = 0
    except BaseException:
        traceback.print_exc()
        code = 1
    finally:
        sys.stdout.flush()
        sys.stderr.flush()
    os._exit(code)


def lease_refusal(dry):
    """None, or the line the ship's lease refuses this caller with (the header's "A ship's lease"). The
    ship is the caller's DISPATCH_SHIP: a launch acting for a leased ship is the skipper's, the yard's
    or the owner's, never a former holder's. leaselib is helm's, found through the core's tool() beside
    helmlib; absent, the launch goes on as it did before S4."""
    ship = next((os.environ[n] for n in ("DISPATCH_SHIP", "DISPATCH_PLAN") if os.environ.get(n)), None)
    if not ship:
        return None
    lib = common.tool("leaselib.py")
    if not lib:
        return None
    if str(lib.parent) not in sys.path:
        sys.path.append(str(lib.parent))   # appended: helm's bin/ never shadows this module's own
    try:
        import leaselib
    except Exception as e:  # a helm that will not load is a line, never the launch's crash
        print("autofinish-run: the lease of ship %s not checked — helm's leaselib does not load (%s)" % (ship, e), file=sys.stderr)
        return None
    return leaselib.fence(ship, "autofinish-run", record=not dry)


# who may type `--by ship` (S6, the header's "A ship's launch"): the yard's tick, never a session. Each
# name marks a caller that is not it — a session, a dispatched run, a skipper, a ship's block
SHIP_NOT_TICK = ("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID", "CLAUDE_UNATTENDED", "SKIPPER_SCOPE", "DISPATCH_SHIP", "DISPATCH_PLAN")


def ship_caller_refusal(environ=None):
    """None when the caller may carry the keel's yes (`--by ship`), else why not: the flag stands for a
    person's yes, so an unattended caller is refused it (AGENTS.md's trap), and the tick under launchd
    is the one caller with none of these set."""
    env = os.environ if environ is None else environ
    for n in SHIP_NOT_TICK:
        if env.get(n):
            return "--by ship is the yard's tick's, and this caller is not it (%s=%s)" % (n, str(env[n])[:40])
    depth = (env.get("DISPATCH_DEPTH") or "0").strip()
    if depth != "0":
        return "--by ship is the yard's tick's, and this caller is a dispatched run (DISPATCH_DEPTH=%s)" % depth[:10]
    return None


def _helm_and_blueprints():
    """(helmlib, blueprintlib) — helm's, found as lease_refusal finds leaselib, and this module's own —
    or raises ImportError naming what is missing."""
    lib = common.tool("helmlib.py")
    if not lib:
        raise ImportError("helm's helmlib.py is not installed")
    if str(lib.parent) not in sys.path:
        sys.path.append(str(lib.parent))
    if HERE not in sys.path:
        sys.path.insert(0, HERE)
    import helmlib
    import blueprintlib
    return helmlib, blueprintlib


def same_repo(path, key):
    """True when PATH (a checkout, a task's repo) is the repo registry KEY names: the keys equal, or, for a
    repo outside the projects folder (a key that is its own absolute path), the same folder resolved."""
    mine = common.repo_key(path)
    if not mine or not key:
        return False
    if mine == key:
        return True
    return mine.startswith("/") and key.startswith("/") and os.path.realpath(mine) == os.path.realpath(key)


def ship_refusal(t, digest):
    """None when DIGEST pins one un-ended ship on this Mac whose keel said merge and whose blocks own
    T's branch, else why the keel's yes cannot be read (the header's "A ship's launch")."""
    if not digest or not re.match(r"^[0-9a-f]{64}$", digest):
        return "--by ship needs --digest D, the ship's pinned digest (64 hex)"
    try:
        helmlib, blueprintlib = _helm_and_blueprints()
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — what cannot be read is no yes
        return "--by ship: the keel's yes cannot be read (%s)" % e
    hits = []
    for pid in helmlib.list_plans():
        p = helmlib.load_plan(pid) or {}
        for name, rec in sorted((p.get("blueprints") or {}).items()):
            pin = rec.get("pin") if isinstance(rec, dict) else None
            if isinstance(pin, dict) and pin.get("digest") == digest and not rec.get("ended"):
                hits.append((pid, name, rec, p))
    if not hits:
        return "--by ship: no un-ended ship on this Mac is pinned at %s" % digest[:12]
    if len(hits) > 1:
        return "--by ship: %d ships are pinned at %s (%s) — which keel said yes cannot be told" % (
            len(hits), digest[:12], ", ".join("%s/%s" % (h[0], h[1]) for h in hits))
    pid, name, rec, plan = hits[0]
    where = "ship %s of plan %s" % (name, pid)
    try:
        bp = blueprintlib.load(rec.get("file") or "", key=rec["pin"].get("repo"), accepted=(digest,))
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — BlueprintError, OSError: the pinned text is the yes
        return "--by ship: %s's pinned copy does not read (%s)" % (where, str(e)[:160] or type(e).__name__)
    if blueprintlib.digest(bp) != digest:
        return "--by ship: %s's pinned copy %s is not at %s" % (where, rec.get("file"), digest[:12])
    if blueprintlib.merge_of(bp["meta"]) == "no":
        return "--by ship: %s's blueprint says merge: no at %s" % (where, digest[:12])
    mode = (rec.get("laid_by") or {}).get("mode") if isinstance(rec.get("laid_by"), dict) else None
    if mode != "attended":
        return "--by ship: %s was laid %s, and only an attended lay is a person's yes" % (where, mode or "by nobody recorded")
    keel = rec.get("merge") if isinstance(rec.get("merge"), dict) else {}
    if keel.get("value") == "no":
        return "--by ship: %s's keel said no (merge no: %s)" % (where, keel.get("why"))
    if not same_repo(t.primary, rec["pin"].get("repo")):
        return "--by ship: %s is not in %s's repo %s" % (t.path, where, rec["pin"].get("repo"))
    here = helmlib.host()
    tasks = plan.get("tasks") or {}
    mine = {blueprintlib.branch_of(bp, st, here) for st in bp["blocks"]}
    mine |= {x.get("seeded_branch") for k, x in tasks.items() if isinstance(x, dict) and x.get("ship") == name
             and (not x.get("repo") or same_repo(x["repo"], rec["pin"].get("repo")))}
    if t.branch not in mine - {None}:
        return "--by ship: %s is no block branch of %s" % (t.branch, where)
    return None


def main(argv):
    if argv[:1] == ["notify"]:
        return notify(argv[1:])
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="autofinish-run", description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
    ap.add_argument("worktree")
    ap.add_argument("--rule", choices="ABCDELM", default="C")
    ap.add_argument("--by", choices=("sweep", "override", "typed", "yolo", "dnd", "chain", "ship"), default="override")
    ap.add_argument("--merge", action="store_true",
                    help="carry the owner's /finish --merge into the run (--by override|typed, or ship with --digest)")
    ap.add_argument("--hold", action="store_true", help="stop at a ready PR whatever the mode: the keel's no (S6)")
    ap.add_argument("--digest", metavar="D", help="--by ship's: the ship's pinned digest, whose keel said merge")
    ap.add_argument("--session", metavar="ID", help="the caller's own session: its lock is no refusal")
    ap.add_argument("--dry", action="store_true")
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if args.merge and args.by not in MERGE_BY:
        print("autofinish-run: --merge needs a person's yes, so --by %s (not %s) only" % (" or ".join(MERGE_BY), args.by),
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    for n in ("CLAUDE_UNATTENDED", "SKIPPER_SCOPE"):
        if args.merge and os.environ.get(n):
            print("autofinish-run: --merge needs a person's yes, and this caller is an unattended run (%s=%s)"
                  % (n, os.environ[n]), file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    if args.merge and args.hold:
        print("autofinish-run: --merge and --hold ask opposite things: one of them", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if args.digest and not (args.by == "ship" and args.merge):
        print("autofinish-run: --digest goes with --merge --by ship", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if args.by == "ship":
        why = ship_caller_refusal() or (None if args.merge or args.hold else
                                        "--by ship is the tick's landing call: --merge --digest D, or --hold")
        if why:
            print("autofinish-run: %s" % why, file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    why = lease_refusal(args.dry)
    if why:
        print("autofinish-run: %s" % why, file=sys.stderr)
        return 4
    t = Tree(os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(args.worktree)))
    bad = t.problem()
    if bad:
        print("autofinish-run: %s: %s" % (args.worktree, bad), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if args.by == "ship" and args.merge:
        why = ship_refusal(t, args.digest)
        if why:
            print("autofinish-run: %s" % why, file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    # --dry writes nothing, the start lock included: it only says what a start would meet
    held = None if args.dry else take_start_lock(t)
    if not args.dry and not held:
        why = "another start on this worktree is under way (%s)" % os.path.join(t.state_dir, START_LOCK)
        print("autofinish-run: not starting %s — %s" % (t.branch, why), file=sys.stderr)
        log("%s run %s %s refused tip=%s rule=%s by=%s — %s" % (now_iso(), t.repo, t.branch, t.tip[:7],
                                                                args.rule, args.by, why))
        return 3
    try:
        return start(t, args)
    finally:
        if held:
            try:
                os.remove(held)
            except OSError:
                pass


def start(t, args):
    """The refusals, the writes and the detach, under the start lock main() holds."""
    prev = read_state(t)
    why = refusal(t, prev, args.by) or lock_refusal(t, args.session, args.by == "typed")
    if why:
        print("autofinish-run: not starting %s — %s" % (t.branch, why), file=sys.stderr)
        if not args.dry:
            log("%s run %s %s refused tip=%s rule=%s by=%s — %s" % (now_iso(), t.repo, t.branch, t.tip[:7],
                                                                    args.rule, args.by, why))
        return 3
    try:
        # cached for --dry, and for a typed hand-off: cold_prompt waits 45 s on this, in a prompt hook.
        # Before the warm run's end below: a run no account can take ends nothing
        label, cfg, picked = account_pick(t, cached=args.dry or args.by == "typed")
    except NoAccount as e:
        why = "no account may run this now — %s" % e
        print("autofinish-run: not starting %s — %s" % (t.branch, why), file=sys.stderr)
        if not args.dry:
            log("%s run %s %s refused tip=%s rule=%s by=%s — %s" % (now_iso(), t.repo, t.branch, t.tip[:7],
                                                                    args.rule, args.by, why))
        return 3
    # A seeded run of this branch is kept the cache's hour, past autofinish's 40 min: it is ended
    # first, then the branch launches (the owner, D2 of docs/dispatch-warm-hour-2026-10-08.md: C). A busy
    # one is not the launch's to end: no launch.
    # Under the start lock and the sweep's RUNNER_TIMEOUT (both 120 s): ending a run takes ~15 s
    # with its window out of view (close tries, the SIGTERM wait, CLOSE_WAIT), so 90 s, and a
    # timeout is a refusal — the next sweep tries again (re-review of 2026-10-08). A typed hand-off
    # gets 30 s: cold_prompt kills this process at 45 s, and a refusal lets the /finish run in its tab.
    warm_s = 30 if args.by == "typed" else 90
    try:
        warm = subprocess.run([sys.executable, os.path.join(HERE, "dispatch-rc"), "end-warm", t.branch, t.primary]
                              + (["--dry-run"] if args.dry else []), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=warm_s)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        warm = subprocess.CompletedProcess([], 1, "", "ending its warm run took over %d s" % warm_s)
    if warm.stdout.strip():
        print(warm.stdout.strip())
    if warm.returncode:
        why = "its dispatch run could not be ended first: " + (warm.stdout.strip() or warm.stderr.strip()[-200:])
        print("autofinish-run: not starting %s — %s" % (t.branch, why), file=sys.stderr)
        if not args.dry:
            log("%s run %s %s refused tip=%s rule=%s by=%s — %s" % (now_iso(), t.repo, t.branch, t.tip[:7],
                                                                    args.rule, args.by, why))
        return 3
    use_account(cfg)
    sid = str(uuid.uuid4())
    # A chain relaunch of a yolo launch is a yolo launch again (chain-manager E3; bin/autofinish's
    # runner_by() keeps a died yolo retry yolo for the same reason): a plain /finish --unattended
    # would merge the answers yolo took where the yolo run stops at a held PR. Recorded as `yolo`,
    # so start_cmd, runner_by and the next chain relaunch all read it as one; CHAIN and the log's
    # `via=chain` say the tick started it.
    by = (prev or {}).get("by") if args.by == "chain" and (prev or {}).get("by") in LAND_BY else args.by
    via = " via=chain" if args.by == "chain" else ""
    hold, mode, eff = landing(t, by, args.rule)
    # the keel's no (S6): a mode that would merge is not asked, and a later launch of this worktree —
    # the sweep's retry of a held run that died starts `--by sweep`, no --hold — keeps it. Its own key,
    # not the text of `hold`: a launch that another rule held first (mode ask) records that rule's
    # reason, and the keel's no must outlive it (S6's finish review)
    keel_hold = bool(args.hold or (prev or {}).get("keel_hold") or (prev or {}).get("hold") == SHIP_HOLD)
    if keel_hold and not hold:
        hold = SHIP_HOLD
    if hold and args.merge:
        args.merge = False   # a held launch merges nothing: no `--merge` in its prompt or state beside `--hold`
    st = {"started": now_iso(), "session": sid, "tip": t.tip, "by": by, "rule": args.rule,
          "window": t.window, "account": label, "ended": None, "outcome": None, "pr": None, "gate": None,
          "merge": args.merge, "hold": hold, "keel_hold": keel_hold, "eff_mode": eff}
    cmd = start_cmd(t, sid, by=by, merge=args.merge, hold=hold)
    try:
        targets = open_sessions(t, args.session, args.by == "typed")
    except Exception as e:  # who to tell is never worth the launch: notify then sends nothing
        targets = []
        print("autofinish-run: the sessions open on %s were not read — %s" % (t.branch, e), file=sys.stderr)
    if args.dry:
        print("autofinish-run --dry: %s in %s, tip %s, rule %s, by %s%s" % (t.branch, t.path, t.tip[:7], args.rule, by, via))
        print("mode %s: %s" % (mode or "none", "held at a ready PR — " + hold if hold else "may merge, past the check and the review gate"))
        print("account %s%s: %s" % (label or "unchanged", " (%s)" % cfg if cfg else "", picked))
        print("would write %s:" % os.path.join(t.state_dir, STATE))
        print("  " + json.dumps(contract(st), ensure_ascii=False))
        print("would write %s: session %s" % (os.path.join(t.state_dir, common.OWNER_FILE), sid))
        print("would write %s: tell %s" % (os.path.join(t.state_dir, NOTIFY), ", ".join(x[:8] for x in targets) or "nobody"))
        text = bundle_text(t)
        print("would write %s (%d characters), beginning:" % (os.path.join(t.state_dir, BUNDLE), len(text)))
        print("\n".join("  | " + l for l in text.splitlines()[:6]))
        print("would run, detached, output to %s:" % t.runlog)
        print("  " + " ".join(shlex.quote(c) for c in cmd))
        print("dispatch --start --dry-run says the session would be:")
        sys.stdout.flush()
        return subprocess.call(start_cmd(t, sid, dry=True, by=by, merge=args.merge, hold=hold), env=start_env(t))
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(t.state_dir, common.OWNER_FILE)) as f:
            before = f.read()
    except OSError:
        before = None
    write_state(t, st)
    try:
        write_targets(t, sid, targets)
    except OSError as e:  # never worth the launch: notify then finds no file and sends nothing
        print("autofinish-run: %s not written — %s" % (NOTIFY, e), file=sys.stderr)
    common.write_owner(t.state_dir, sid, t.branch)
    if args.by == "chain":   # counted before the detach: a start that fails is refused, which chain_refusal skips
        tmp = os.path.join(t.state_dir, "%s.%d" % (CHAIN, os.getpid()))
        with open(tmp, "w") as f:
            json.dump({"tip": t.tip, "sessions": chain_spent(t, prev) + [sid]}, f)
        os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(t.state_dir, CHAIN))
    log("%s run %s %s started session=%s tip=%s rule=%s by=%s%s account=%s window=\"%s\" — %s" % (
        st["started"], t.repo, t.branch, sid[:8], t.tip[:7], args.rule, by, via + (" merge=yes" if args.merge else "")
        + (" hold=\"%s\"" % hold if hold else ""),
        label or "-", t.window, picked))
    try:
        detach(lambda: wait_for_end(t, st, cmd), t.runlog)
    except OSError as e:
        # no child: a lock naming a session that never exists would refuse the panel for 2 h
        give_back(t, sid, before, st)
        print("autofinish-run: %s did not start — %s; the lock is given back" % (t.branch, e), file=sys.stderr)
        log("%s run %s %s never-started gate=%s session=%s tip=%s rule=%s by=%s — the detach failed: %s" % (
            st["ended"], t.repo, t.branch, REFUSED, sid[:8], t.tip[:7], args.rule, by, e))
        return 1
    print("started: %s — window and Remote Control \"%s\", session %s, account %s; state %s; log %s"
          % (finish_prompt(t.branch, by, args.merge, hold), t.window, sid, label or "unchanged", os.path.join(t.state_dir, STATE), t.runlog))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
